ey to releasing and  controlling the augiejhu jihad  even if Hellboy himself would rather not  be on that it's also a big heavy hand  that he can use to hit monsters with and  more recent comic book stories Hellboy  has assumed greater control over his  demonic form to the point that he can  manipulate his own size and even sprout  wings and pull horns when he wishes  although this is generally not an  ability explored in film versions of the  character yet in the 2019 Hellboy milla  jovovich plays Nimue a originally known  as the Lady of the lake  Nimmo a is a being from Arthurian legend  that was a powerful witch and extremely  close to Merlin Merlin told her all of  his magical secrets but she ultimately  imprisoned him and went mad with the  dark knowledge she was eventually killed  when all the other witches of Britain  banded together to kill her and seal her  body deep in a tomb in the comics story  The Wild Hunt  Nemo a is resurrected after she's  nominated to become the leader of The  Witches of Britain many of whom flee and  terror from her power it's during this  storyline that Morgana lafay reveals to  Hellboy that he's actually the last heir  of King Arthur setting up a showdown  between Hellboy and Nimmo a that could  bring about the end of the world suffice  it to say Nemo way is bad news indeed  Hellboy wouldn't be who he is without  Professor Trevor Broome the man who  found and essentially adopted him in  1944 when he first appeared on earth  broom is an English a cult expert who  began working with Allied forces in  world war ii when it became clear that  the nazis were planning to call demonic  forces to earth after the war broom  helped form the Bureau of paranormal  research and defense and he and Hellboy  battled various occult threats together  until brooms retirements as director of  the agency in the comics broom was  killed in 1994 by a frog monster tied to  the augiejhu jihad and had a similarly  gruesome end in 2004 Hellboy movie  he was played by John Hertz in both the  original and 2008 Hellboy 2 the Golden  Army and is played by Ian McShane in the  2019 film throughout his comic book and  cinematic history  Hellboy has retained close ties to the  Bureau of paranormal research and  defense for BPRD the bureau's mission  statement is right there in its name  there are things that go bump in the  night  aging mind's eye no mistake about that  and we are the ones who pump back it's  job is the research and combat various  occult threats and phenomenon that may  pose a threat to humanity often with the  aid of various supernatural entities and  humans who have been gifted with special  abilities Hellboy is the most  predominant of these members but the  Bureau has also included members like  the fish man Abe Sapien and the  pyrokinetic human Elizabeth Sherman and  a 2009 teen film the BPRD also includes  Ben daimyo a BPRD agent who was killed  by a Jaguar cult on assignment in  Bolivia daimyo rose from the dead and  has since manifested the ability to  transform into a jaguar creature in  november of 2018 a last-minute casting  edition was announced for the new  Hellboy film Thomas Haden Church joined  the reboot as lobster Johnson a  character created by Mike manola in 1999  as an homage to various pulp heroes of  the early 20th century in the comics the  lobster was a vigilante and depression  heir in New York City known for burning  his lobster emblem into the flesh of  criminals to the public he was thought  to be an urban legend and eventually a  fictional character dreamed up by a pulp  writer instead the lobster was real  enough to begin working for the US  government in the late 1930s in an  effort to thwart various Nazi missions  he died in 1939 while attempting to stop  a Nazi space launch that would have  possibly put the Third Reich into space  in 2001 he appeared in the Conqueror  worm storyline as a ghost who haunts the  ruins of the castle where he died he's  made occasional appearances in the  comics since leading a ghostly helping  hand to the BPRD against supernatural  threats the first two Hellboy films were  mastermind by director Guillermo del  Toro with Ron Perlman in the title role  Hellboy 2 the Golden Army ends with a  hint for more Hellboy story to come  unfortunately the film under  performed and a planned third movie  didn't materialize as years went by del  Toro continued to express interest but  in early 2017 he announced that all  efforts had finally been exhausted  months later the reboot was announced  without del Toro attached  according to Hellboy creator Mike  Minneola there was some talk of trying  to continue del Toro story with a new  film but he felt that wouldn't be fair  to a new team of filmmakers he told  sci-fi that he was looking forward to  director Neil Marshalls take in the  summer of 2017 the Hellboy reboot  ignited an uproar with a casting  announcement ed skrein was confirmed to  play Ben daimyo in the comics daimyo is  a Japanese American and this heritage  plays a major role in both his life and  in the BPRD comics stories fans were  confused and upset that the production  didn't cast a Japanese American actor to  better to pick the character on screen  scrying became aware of the outcry after  taking the role and released a statement  saying he would be departing the  production to make room for another  actor then in September 2017 Korean  American actor Daniel Dae Kim signed on  to play the role of Ben daimyo thanks to  the cast and crew's willingness to  correct themselves we got a Ben daimyo  who looks more like the Ben that fans  were introduced to on the comics page  both of Hellboy's previous big-screen  adventures were pg-13 rated fantasy  adventures with certain horror elements  however in 2017 Hellboy director Neil  Marshall remarked that he had been  granted permission to take the film into  our rated territory what she saw not as  a mandate but as a license to depict the  same level of violence 